# A single-backtick template string: literal text runs and {curly} substitution
# sections, delimited by ` marker args. Escapes (\` \{ \} \\) produce literals.
say `hello {name} world`
say `escaped \{braces\} and \`backtick\``

$ facts
$ assert sentence say (`) (hello ) { name } ( world) (`)
$ assert sentence say (`) (escaped {braces} and `backtick`) (`)